       NON-COMMERCIAL COMPONENTS. These files wrap CUDA kernels written by
       Simon Niklaus and published in repositories whose README states: "The
       provided implementation is strictly for academic purposes only. Should
       you be interested in using our technology for any commercial use,
       please feel free to contact us."
         - cupy_ops/softsplat.py   https://github.com/sniklaus/softmax-splatting
         - cupy_ops/sepconv.py     https://github.com/sniklaus/pytorch-sepconv
         - cupy_ops/costvol.py, cupy_ops/correlation.py
           these appear to come from Niklaus' PyTorch re-implementations of
           optical-flow networks (for example sniklaus/pytorch-pwc), based on
           their coding style and kernel names. Their READMEs say the underlying
           models are free for non-commercial use only. The exact origin was not
           verified.
         - cupy_ops/batch_edt.py   origin not identified; treat as unverified.
       These repositories carry no licence file. Treat these files as
       restricted to academic and personal, non-commercial use, and cite:
         S. Niklaus and F. Liu, "Softmax Splatting for Video Frame
         Interpolation", CVPR 2020, https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.05534

       cupy_ops/adacof.py is derived from https://github.com/HyeongminLEE/AdaCoF-pytorch
       (MIT, see LICENSES/AdaCoF-pytorch-MIT.txt).

       Only softsplat.py is used by the GMFSS pipeline at run time. The other
       kernels are carried over from the ComfyUI package and are not needed.


3. MODEL WEIGHTS (not included in this repository)

   src/download_models.py fetches the GMFSS Fortuna checkpoints at setup time
   from https://github.com/styler00dollar/VSGAN-tensorrt-docker/releases (that
   repository is BSD-3-Clause). The weights come from
   https://github.com/98mxr/GMFSS_Fortuna and are distributed by their authors
   for research and personal use. Their terms apply to the weights, not the
   MIT licence of this project. Verify them before commercial use.


4. EXTERNAL TOOLS (downloaded, not included)

   ffmpeg (GPL build from gyan.dev, fetched by setup.bat) and optionally
   MKVToolNix (GPL-2.0). They run as separate programs and are not linked into
   this project.


5. PYTHON DEPENDENCIES (installed, not included)

   PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), CuPy (MIT) and the NVIDIA CUDA
